 # Jiang et al. Acceleration Structure
 Also called: JRZ*16 method
+
 ## Overview
-The Jiang et al. acceleration structure [JRZ*16] is a hierarchical data structure designed to efficiently locate active cells within a scalar volume for both direct and indirect visualization approaches [S1]. It solves the problem of redundant ray marching through inactive background regions by identifying and rendering only the relevant active cells [S1]. Unlike pure image-order methods, it is classified as a hybrid object-order and image-order approach, meaning its performance and structure are dependent on the rendering resolution [S1]. It builds on [Hierarchical Data Structures](4133-hierarchical-data-structures.md) and differs from [Hierarchical Spatial Enumeration Optimization](1663-hierarchical-spatial-enumeration-optimization.md) and [Silhouette Image Space Acceleration Structure (Mip Pyramid)](3731-silhouette-image-space-acceleration-structure-mip-pyramid.md) by relying on resolution-dependent hybrid traversal rather than pure image-order or object-order enumeration [G].
